     "notes": {
      "text": "Black's e5 pawn is undefended. 2.Nf3 attacks it while developing a piece, also eyes d4 and prepares castling; it is by far the most popular move. 2.f4 (King's Gambit) and 2.d4 attack with pawns instead. 2.Qh5 or 2.Qf3 hope for a quick mate, but if Black stays calm they are not dangerous.",
