     "notes": {
      "text": "3...a6 puts the question to the bishop: take or retreat, but it cannot stay. 4.Bxc6, the Exchange Variation, does not win e5 yet, because after 4...dxc6 5.Nxe5? Qd4! Black forks knight and pawn. 4.Ba4 is the main line: it keeps the bishop and the pressure on the knight. Watch out later for ...b5 and ...c4 trapping a bishop on b3.",
      "credit": {
       "source": "Wikibooks, Chess Opening Theory/1. e4/1...e5/2. Nf3/2...Nc6/3. Bb5/3...a6",
       "url": "https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Chess_Opening_Theory/1._e4/1...e5/2._Nf3/2...Nc6/3._Bb5/3...a6",
       "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
