     "notes": {
      "text": "4...Nf6 develops and attacks e4. 5.O-O is the main line: castle to safety and get ready for Re1, leaving e4 to look after itself. If 5...Nxe4 (the Open Spanish), 6.d4 wins the pawn back. 5.d3 or 5.Nc3 defend e4 directly but get in the way of White's plan of c3 and d4.",
      "credit": {
