     "notes": {
      "text": "5...Be7, the Closed Spanish, guards the king along the e-file. Now Black really threatens ...b5 and ...Nxe4, winning the pawn. 6.Re1 defends e4 with a developing move. 6.Qe2 also holds it, but puts the queen on a file likely to open; 6.d3 and 6.Nc3 get in the way of c3 and d4.",
